{"id": 3025, "title": "“万” Is Hard to Write", "level": "Intermediate", "hsk_tags": ["HSK3"], "slug": "wan-is-hard-to-write", "audio_url": "/audio/mandarin/3025_wan-is-hard-to-write.mp3", "simplified_paragraphs": ["从前，有个商人聘请了一位老师教他儿子认字。第一天上学，老师用笔在纸上写了一笔，说：”这是个‘一’字。”他儿子学得很认真。第二天上学，老师又在纸上写了两笔，说：\"这是个’二’字。”第三天，老师在纸上写了三笔，说：\"这是个‘三’字。”儿子觉得写字很简单，自己已经学会写字了，就请父亲辞退了老师。过了几天，商人让儿子写\"万\"字，可是写了一天也没写好，儿子说：\"’万‘字竟然这么难写，我写了一天才写了3000划。”", "知识是无穷无尽的，如果我们学习只满足于一知半解，那和这个笨儿子又有什么区别呢？"], "traditional_paragraphs": ["從前，有個商人聘請了一位老師教他兒子認字。第一天上學，老師用筆在紙上寫了一筆，說：”這是個‘一’字。”他兒子學得很認真。第二天上學，老師又在紙上寫了兩筆，說：\"這是個’二’字。”第三天，老師在紙上寫了三筆，說：\"這是個‘三’字。”兒子覺得寫字很簡單，自己已經學會寫字了，就請父親辭退了老師。過了幾天，商人讓兒子寫\"萬\"字，可是寫了一天也沒寫好，兒子說：\"’萬‘字竟然這麼難寫，我寫了一天才寫了3000劃。”", "知識是無窮無盡的，如果我們學習只滿足於一知半解，那和這個笨兒子又有什麼區別呢？"], "pinyin_paragraphs": ["cóng qián， yǒu gè shāng rén pìn qǐng le yī wèi lǎo shī jiāo tā ér zi rèn zì。 dì yī tiān shàng xué， lǎo shī yòng bǐ zài zhǐ shàng xiě le yī bǐ， shuō：” zhè shì gè‘ yī’ zì。” tā ér zi xué de hěn rèn zhēn。 dì èr tiān shàng xué， lǎo shī yòu zài zhǐ shàng xiě le liǎng bǐ， shuō：\" zhè shì gè’ èr’ zì。” dì sān tiān， lǎo shī zài zhǐ shàng xiě le sān bǐ， shuō：\" zhè shì gè‘ sān’ zì。” ér zi jué de xiě zì hěn jiǎn dān， zì jǐ yǐ jīng xué huì xiě zì le， jiù qǐng fù qīn cí tuì le lǎo shī。 guò le jǐ tiān， shāng rén ràng ér zi xiě \" wàn \" zì， kě shì xiě le yī tiān yě méi xiě hǎo， ér zi shuō：\"’ wàn‘ zì jìng rán zhè me nán xiě， wǒ xiě le yī tiān cái xiě le 3000 huà。”", "zhī shi shì wú qióng wú jìn de， rú guǒ wǒ men xué xí zhǐ mǎn zú yú yī zhī bàn jiě， nà hé zhè gè bèn ér zi yòu yǒu shén me qū bié ne？"], "english_paragraphs": ["Once, a merchant hired a teacher to teach his son Chinese characters. On the first day, the teacher drew one stroke on a piece of paper and said, “This is the character ‘一’ (one).” The boy studied hard. On the second day, the teacher drew two strokes and said, “This is ‘二’ (two).” On the third day, he drew three strokes and said, “This is ‘三’ (three).” The boy decided writing was easy and that he had already learned how to do it, so he asked his father to dismiss the teacher. A few days later, the merchant asked his son to write “万” (ten thousand). The boy worked on it all day but still could not finish. “Who knew ‘万’ would be so hard to write?” he said. “I’ve been writing all day, and I’ve only managed 3,000 strokes.”", "There is no end to what we can learn. If we are content with only a little understanding, how are we any different from this foolish son?"], "english_full": "Once, a merchant hired a teacher to teach his son Chinese characters. On the first day, the teacher drew one stroke on a piece of paper and said, “This is the character ‘一’ (one).” The boy studied hard. On the second day, the teacher drew two strokes and said, “This is ‘二’ (two).” On the third day, he drew three strokes and said, “This is ‘三’ (three).” The boy decided writing was easy and that he had already learned how to do it, so he asked his father to dismiss the teacher. A few days later, the merchant asked his son to write “万” (ten thousand). The boy worked on it all day but still could not finish. “Who knew ‘万’ would be so hard to write?” he said. “I’ve been writing all day, and I’ve only managed 3,000 strokes.”\n\nThere is no end to what we can learn. If we are content with only a little understanding, how are we any different from this foolish son?", "ruby_paragraphs": ["<ruby class=\"mb-tooltip\" data-py=\"cóng qián\" data-defn=\"previously / formerly / once upon a time\" data-hsk=\"HSK 5\"><span class=\"si\">从前</span><span class=\"tr\">從前</span><rt>cóng qián</rt></ruby>，<ruby class=\"mb-tooltip\" data-py=\"yǒu\" data-defn=\"to have; there is\" data-hsk=\"HSK 1\"><span class=\"si\">有</span><span class=\"tr\">有</span><rt>yǒu</rt></ruby><ruby class=\"mb-tooltip\" data-py=\"gè\" data-defn=\"classifier for people or objects in general\" data-hsk=\"HSK 1\"><span class=\"si\">个</span><span class=\"tr\">個</span><rt>gè</rt></ruby><ruby class=\"mb-tooltip\" data-py=\"shāng rén\" data-defn